<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Pechina</h1><p class="st-meta">884 CE – 922 CE (approx.) · capital Pechina</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A self-governing community of Andalusi sailors near Almería that traded across the Mediterranean and founded Oran in 902.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 884 a community of Andalusi seafarers, the bahriyyun, settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechina">Bajjana</a> (Pechina) in the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andarax">Andarax</a> valley near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a>, with the permission of the emir and alongside local Arab families. They formed a self-governing body during the decline of central authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechina">Pechina</a> was run by a council of sailors rather than a single ruler, recognising the emir only nominally. It lived from maritime trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, and its sailors founded trading posts on the African coast, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> in 902. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> served as its harbour and watchtower, and the town grew wealthy as a port for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechina">Pechina</a> under direct control around 922. Its harbour, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a>, then eclipsed it, becoming the main naval base of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba</a>, and Pechina declined into a village.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 884 CE – 922 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.29%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>884 CE – 922 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pechina</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bajjana, Maritime Republic of Pechina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=903&amp;focus=republic-of-pechina" aria-label="Republic of Pechina on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4619 848 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Pechina lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4939 1104L4881 1071"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 1071h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4939 1104h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4939 1104h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pechina. <a href="/atlas?year=903&amp;focus=republic-of-pechina">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
